{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$f(x)$ is the product of two, more basic, expressions: $x^2$ and $e^x$.\n\nTherefore, the derivative of $f$ can be found using **the product rule**:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)v(x)]\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)]v(x)+u(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}[v(x)]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=u'(x)v(x)+u(x)v'(x)\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}f'(x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^2e^x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^2)e^x+x^2\\dfrac{d}{dx}(e^x)\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{The product rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=2x\\cdot e^x+x^2\\cdot e^x\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Differentiate }x^2\\text{ and }e^x}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=xe^x(2+x)\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Simplify}}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$f'(x)= xe^x(x+2)$\n\nor any other equivalent form.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $f(x)=x^2e^x$.\n\n$f'(x)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"2xe^x+x^2e^x"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
